      "analysis": [
        "There IS order to the chaos, but it is priority-driven freestyle, not fixed combos — exactly what the Discord playstyle section teaches (rotate protected CCs and ranged DPS, stay protected, clone-swap). The taught full combos almost never appear verbatim; pieces of the combo families show up as the situation allows.",
        "The constant Spirit Step weaving is protection upkeep, not just movement: in PvP, Spirit Step gives Invincible → Super Armor (nullified during its cooldown), so dashing between every cast keeps a protection layer rolling while CC skills come off cooldown.",
        "The visible loop: cycle protected pokes — Bristling Sparks (SA, stun), Flower Shroud (FG, stun), Petalblast (SA), Petal Snare (FG) — from safe range while weaving Spirit Step, and fish for a hit. Charmed is the exception he risks up close: unprotected, but its stiff starts the punish. Burst only gets committed after a confirmed catch: Charmed → Foxflare → Heavenward Dance, a shortened Stiff/Foxflare-family punish.",
        "Openers come from range behind protection: the match opener was Spirit Step weave → Petalblast (SA poke — its Bound is PvE-only) → Bared Claws → Spirited Away → Bristling Sparks; fragment 3 also opens on Petalblast. This matches the Discord line that Succession PvP centres on long-range AoE CCs into melee burst.",
        "Fragment 3 (Petalblast → Lurking → Soulsnare → Flow: Hanpuri → Heavenward → Spirit Swirl) is recognisably the Hanpuri family shape with a different opener; fragments 2 and 4 are repositioning/DPS glue, not combos.",
        "The displayed addons are the current #1's evasion build, and they're built entirely around the accuracy/evasion war that decides capped fights: he pumps his own evasion (Spirit Swirl +20 Eva, on a rotatable SA skill) while crushing enemy accuracy (Heavenward -20 Acc) and evasion (Foxflare -20 Eva). Self crit sits on Bared Claws — his most-woven cancel tool, so a buff there has near-100% uptime for free; the finishers (Spirited Away, Heavenward) carry the conditional Down/Back-attack bonuses. Contrast the earlier DR #1, whose addons were raw-crit flavored with the -DR/-Eva debuff on Bared Claws instead.",
        "Recurring micro-chains inside the freestyle (the only sequences that repeat): Flower Shroud → Bristling (3×, the poke pair), Bared Claws → Petal Play (2×, a taught cancel), Petal Play → Foxflare → Foxspirit Tag (2×, the -20 DP debuff applied right after the KD attempt), and Heavenward Dance as the burst ender after whichever connector landed (Foxflare / Lurking / Hanpuri, 3×). Long sequences never repeat — priorities pick the next cast, these cells drop in when the moment fits.",
        "The clone swap (Foxspirit: Deceiver, Q) was never logged — the one notable divergence from the Discord guidance, which leans hard on clone swaps. It may genuinely be unused, or it's easy to miss: Q is instant and works during other animations."
      ],
      "notes": [
        "After the main log the session repeated the same pool, with constant Spirit Step weaving between casts.",
        "Setup evidence applied to the AOS loadout (2026-06-12, user's call): all three rabams confirmed — 56 Spirit Parade and 57 Petal Snare seen in play, 58 Soul Charm read off his skill-enhancement tree screenshot — plus Petalblast unlocked for AOS.",
        "Lurking Claws, Soulsnare→Hanpuri, Spirit Swirl, Flow: Nether River, and Spirited Away only appeared in the later fragments — not in the main rotation pool first logged.",
        "Path of Petals (W+F) was also seen, used purely for movement (not logged in a sequence).",
        "The match opener (DR-#1 log) is not addon pre-buffing — hypothesis raised and retracted 2026-06-12; it reads as ranged CC fishing while the gap closes.",
        "Not observed (one session — weak evidence): Foxspirit: Deceiver (the clone swap), Foxflare Fling, Heavenly Return, Spirit Sparks."
      ]
    }
